WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.850
Lab 1 runs on a laptop with no tenant.

2
00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:06.700
First, run Learn's queries
over the fictional audit rows.

3
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.446
Eight tests pass, and
the third shows the trap:

4
00:00:09.446 --> 00:00:13.900
two of the rows the first query returns
are assignments made outside PIM.

5
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.225
Next, list the run's permissions.

6
00:00:16.225 --> 00:00:18.625
There are nine, and
none of them can write.

7
00:00:18.625 --> 00:00:21.513
Then run two days against
the fictional tenant.

8
00:00:21.513 --> 00:00:26.028
The second day has three Tier 0
findings: a role assigned outside PIM,

9
00:00:26.028 --> 00:00:29.899
an activation nobody approved,
and a changed role setting.

10
00:00:29.899 --> 00:00:33.890
Open the events file, and
you'll see IDs, not names.
